id: k8s.storage-class
kind: kubernetes
title: StorageClass
aliases: storageclass, provisioner
tags: storage
questions:
  - how does dynamic volume provisioning work?
invariant: A StorageClass names a provisioner plus parameters, so PVCs are satisfied without pre-created volumes.
answer_30s: StorageClass is the template a PVC uses to get a volume created on demand, and it carries the reclaim and binding policy.
answer_2m: |
  `volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer` is the setting worth remembering:
  it delays provisioning until a Pod is scheduled, so the volume is created in
  the same zone as the node. With Immediate binding, a multi-zone cluster can
  schedule a Pod into a zone where its volume cannot be attached, and the Pod
  hangs in ContainerCreating. The second setting is `reclaimPolicy`: Delete
  loses data when the PVC goes away, Retain leaves the PV behind for recovery.
when_to_use:
  - any cluster offering more than one storage tier (SSD, HDD, replicated)
commands:
  - kubectl get storageclass => which provisioners exist and which is default
  - kubectl get pv => reclaim policy per bound volume
failure_modes:
  - Immediate binding with multi-zone nodes, causing unschedulable Pods
  - Delete reclaim policy on data you meant to keep
related:
  - k8s.pvc
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/storage-classes/
